#N canvas 100 100 800 840 10;
#X obj 40 40 jet_win;
#X msg 40 80 create;
#X msg 130 80 destroy;
#X obj 40 130 jet_head 0;
#X obj 40 170 jet_render 512 384;
#X text 180 170 <- left outlet: the scene   right outlet: the result as a texture;
#X obj 40 215 t b b;
#X obj 120 250 f 0;
#X obj 170 250 + 2;
#X msg 120 280 set 0 \$1 0;
#X obj 40 320 jet_rotateXYZ 0 0 0;
#X obj 40 350 jet_color 1 0.5 0.2;
#X obj 40 380 jet_cube 2.5;
#X text 190 380 <- the scene: a spinning cube \, drawn into the texture;
#X obj 380 215 t b b;
#X obj 380 260 jet_separator;
#X obj 380 290 jet_translateXYZ -2.7 0 0;
#X obj 380 320 jet_rectangle 2 1.5;
#X obj 560 260 jet_separator;
#X obj 560 290 jet_translateXYZ 2.7 0 0;
#X obj 560 320 jet_rotateXYZ 20 30 0;
#X obj 560 350 jet_cube 2.2;
#X text 380 380 the same texture on a flat picture and on a cube;
#X msg 40 430 clear 0.1 0.2 0.45 1;
#X msg 210 430 camera 2 2 5;
#X msg 40 458 camera 0 0 4;
#X msg 210 458 fov 50;
#X msg 40 486 fov 90;
#X msg 210 486 resolution 128 96;
#X msg 40 514 resolution 512 384;
#X msg 210 514 readback;
#X text 40 570 [jet_render w h] draws a scene into a texture instead of the window - TouchDesigner's Render TOP. Everything connected to the LEFT outlet is the scene: shapes \, transforms \, colours \, even effects. It is seen through the camera of jet_render (camera \, lookat \, fov and range messages\ \, by default the window's default camera) and lit by the window's light unless you send light / lightcolor. When the scene is done\ \, the RIGHT outlet fires with the result bound as the current texture - use it with a shape\ \, an effect block\ \, jet_shader\ \, jet_share...;
#X text 40 690 The scene starts clean (no transform\ \, white\ \, depth test on\ \, no texture) and the state of the chain above is restored afterwards. Width and height can be set by creation arguments\ \, by the two right inlets (they only store) or by "resolution". "clear r g b a" is the background colour. The scene's aspect ratio is width / height of the texture\ \, independent of the window\ \, so with the default camera [jet_rectangle 5.33 4] fills a 4:3 texture. Scenes can be nested a few levels deep. "readback" prints the colour of two pixels of the result in the Pd window - a quick way to check what is in there.;
